    "created_at": "2025-11-27T12:57:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-11-27T12:57:25Z",
    "body": "> Currently all browsers start loading an image immediately - Perhaps this is an observable implementation decision in all browsers to not create that inert document, rather than something to do with this intermediate fragment?\n\nThat's not the intent. We should parse into an inert doc. My current implementation indeed loads stuff prematurely; I'll get that fixed.\n\nThere used to be a test case for this exact case, but I think we've dropped it when re-doing the test suite. I'll revive that test, too. \n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
